  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Jansson's Temptation is a Swedish gratin of layered potato, onion, preserved anchovies and double cream. It is topped with breadcrumbs and baked until golden and bubbling. Serves 4."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Use Swedish-style preserved anchovies if you can find them; they are sweeter and milder than Mediterranean anchovies in olive oil. Standard tinned anchovies work fine and the result is still excellent."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "ingredientsList",
        "attrs": {
          "defaultServings": 6,
          "items": [
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "potato",
              "amount": 1000,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "peeled, cut into thin matchsticks",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "anchovies",
              "amount": 80,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "tinned, drained",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "onion",
              "amount": 2,
              "unit": "medium",
              "prepNote": "thinly sliced",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "double-cream",
              "amount": 300,
              "unit": "ml",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "unsalted-butter",
              "amount": 20,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "for greasing",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "breadcrumbs-dried",
              "amount": 30,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat the oven to 200°C. Butter the rectangular baking tin generously."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Layer half the potato matchsticks in the tin. Scatter over the sliced onion and lay the anchovy fillets evenly across the surface."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the remaining potato on top. Pour the double cream evenly over the whole dish."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Scatter the breadcrumbs over the surface. Dot with any remaining butter."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Bake for 70 to 75 minutes until the top is golden and a skewer slides through the potato without resistance. Rest for 5 minutes before serving."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "The top browns before the potato is cooked.",
              "solution": "Cover the tin loosely with foil and continue baking. Remove the foil for the last 10 minutes to crisp the crust."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "The cream boils over in the oven.",
              "solution": "Place a baking tray on the shelf below to catch any spills. Do not overfill the tin; the cream should reach just below the potato surface."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "The dish tastes very salty.",
              "solution": "Rinse the anchovy fillets before using them. Some tinned anchovies are heavily salted; rinsing reduces the intensity."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Jansson's Temptation is on every Swedish julbord at Christmas. It sits alongside meatballs, pickled herring and rice pudding on the holiday table. Swedes also make it for Easter and Midsummer. It is a side dish, served in the baking tin at the table."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
